* BP758: 500 mA adjustable low-dropout regulator, SOT-23-5, 0.55 V reference. Behavioural macro-model: a
* transconductance error amplifier with its compensation network driving the gate of a PMOS pass transistor;
* enable threshold 0.9 V.
* No current limit, no thermal shutdown, no noise.
* Written for Backplane's simulation benchmark (test/ksim_bench). It is not a manufacturer's model of any part.
*
* Connections:  input
*               |  ground
*               |  |   enable
*               |  |   |  feedback
*               |  |   |  |  output
*               |  |   |  |  |
.subckt BP758   in gnd en fb out
Bref ref gnd V = v(en,gnd) > 0.9 ? 0.55 : 0
Gea g gnd ref fb 100u
Ro in g 3meg
Rz in gz 120k
Cz gz g 20p
Cg in g 2p
Dlo gnd g BP758_CLAMP
Dhi g in BP758_CLAMP
M1 out g in in BP758_PASS W=1u L=1u
Iq in gnd 50u
.model BP758_PASS PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.7 KP=1.6 LAMBDA=0.02)
.model BP758_CLAMP D (IS=1e-14)
.ends BP758
